  "aiReview": {
    "strengths": {
      "bestArea": "Catch-and-shoot shooting off movement — 46.3% FG on catch-and-shoot jumpers (175 attempts, Excellent/97th percentile), climbing to 54.1% FG when left unguarded (74 attempts). 3PT shooting overall is elite on real volume: 42.4% on 257 attempts.",
      "bestPlayType": "Spot Up — his single largest role (28.8% of possessions, 131 on the season) and graded Very Good (1.069 PPP, 75th percentile). Transition is a close second, actually his most efficient high-volume action (1.219 PPP, Very Good).",
      "overallStrength": "An elite off-ball scorer for a one-season sample: every play type with real volume graded Average or better, and four of his top five (Spot Up, Transition, Off Screen, Handoffs) graded Very Good or Excellent. He punishes teams that leave him — 54.1% FG on unguarded catch-and-shoot looks — and is equally live moving without the ball off screens (94th percentile) as he is spotting up."
    },
    "weaknesses": {
      "worstArea": "Short to 17 shots (short/floater range, outside the immediate rim area) — 25.7% FG on 35 attempts, graded Poor (12th percentile). The one clearly cold zone in an otherwise excellent shooting profile.",
      "worstPlayType": "P&R Ball Handler — his only play type below Good efficiency (0.744 PPP, Average/41st percentile on 43 possessions), though it's a small part of his game (9.5% of possessions) next to his off-ball scoring.",
      "overallWeakness": "His whole profile is built on off-ball scoring and catch-and-shoot efficiency; the two areas that require him to create in tighter spaces off the dribble — the short/floater game and running actual pick-and-roll as the ball handler — are the only parts of his offense that aren't already strong.",
      "developmentTarget": "Adding a reliable in-between/floater game and more comfort as a live-dribble pick-and-roll operator would round out an already elite off-ball scoring profile and make him less matchup-dependent on defenses that take away the catch-and-shoot look."
    }
